this is because Roll and RollBinding are namespaced meaning the user will be having permisions only for the namespace
where Role binding is defined if we try to access resouces in anotehr namesapce we will get an error 
so previously we define the role binding in the default namespace but we are tryying to access the resources from the test namespace in which we did not create the role Binding 

so when we have multiple namespaces defining RoleBinding in every namespace is a TDS Process and Few resources 
like Persistent volumes are not even namespaced for which we cannot add role binding
there must be a way to define Roles and RoleBindings at the cluster level instead of namespace level

that's where cluster Role and Cluster Role Biinding comes into the pictire 
the only difference b/w Role binding and cluster role binding is that RoleBinding is namespaced 
whereas Cluster RoleBinding is at the Cluster level that means they can access the resources in any namespace 

ClusterRole is similer to role 

